Chapter: ProbeScanCost
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter TextSearch

 What does it cost to find 93 names in a program-sized text, in Codex, on the
 venue the plug actually runs on?

 This exists because tree-shaking needs ROOTS, and the obvious way to get them
 is to scan the emitted program for each prelude name. `index-of` is not a
 builtin -- `index-of-loop` walks positions and `text-matches-at-loop` walks
 characters, both at Codex level -- so the obvious way is a naive O(n*m) search
 run 93 times over ~1.9 MB, under QEMU. That is either fine or catastrophic and
 guessing costs a native build to find out.

 So: a FIXED, SMALL amount of the same work, timed from outside, and
 extrapolated. The needles are absent on purpose -- a miss is the worst case, because it
 scans to the end -- and they SHARE THE `cx_` PREFIX the haystack is full of,
 so every position starting `cx_` pays a multi-character compare before it
 fails. A first draft used needles starting `zzz`, which never appears, so each
 position failed on character one and the measurement was the best case rather
 than the worst.

 The result is printed so the work cannot be optimised away.

Section: Instrument

  grow : Text, Integer -> Text
  grow (t) (n) = if n <= 0 then t else grow (t & t) (n - 1)

  hits : Text, List Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  hits (hay) (needles) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length needles then acc
   else when index-of hay (list-at needles i)
    is Just (p) -> hits hay needles (i + 1) (acc + 1)
    is None -> hits hay needles (i + 1) acc

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let base = "fn cx_ll_push(l: anytype, v: anytype) @TypeOf(l) { return l; }\n"
   in let hay = grow base 14
   in let needles = ["cx_ll_pushx", "cx_ll_popx", "cx_text_splitx", "cx_new_x",
        "cx_ll_concatx", "cx_gpa_x", "cx_deck_basex", "cx_heap_memx",
        "cx_char_encodex", "cx_text_comparex", "cx_bits_to_realx", "cx_ipowx",
        "CxListx", "CxFn1x", "CxFn2x", "cx_ll_emptyx",
        "cx_ll_ofx", "cx_ll_insert_atx", "cx_text_to_doublex", "cx_char_to_textx"]
   in act
     print-line-uni ("haystack chars : " & show (text-length hay))
     print-line-uni ("needles        : " & show (list-length needles))
     print-line-uni ("scanned chars  : " & show (text-length hay * list-length needles))
     print-line-uni ("hits (expect 0): " & show (hits hay needles 0 0))
   end
  end
